s said no arrests had been made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The authorities in New Orleans are investigating a shooting that left at least 10 people wounded early on Sunday during a weekend of a popular football game that draws many visitors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/multimedia/01xp-neworleans/01xp-neworleans-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/01/multimedia/01xp-neworleans/01xp-neworleans-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/multimedia/01xp-neworleans/01xp-neworleans-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/multimedia/01xp-neworleans/01xp-neworleans-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/multimedia/01xp-neworleans/01xp-neworleans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/01/multimedia/01xp-neworleans/01xp-neworleans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/01/multimedia/01xp-neworleans/01xp-neworleans-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '10 People Wounded in New Orleans Shooting, Police Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '10 Are Wounded in New Orleans Shooting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-01T14:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Mele', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mele', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e1b2ea3-d424-5ed7-ac8d-785bca89426b', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e1b2ea3-d424-5ed7-ac8d-785bca89426b'}, {'abstract': 'Newly separated and living in her parents’ building, a writer gives stand-up comedy a try. What happened next was not in the script.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/01/arts/television/stand-up-comedy-mrs-maisel.html', 'snippet': 'Newly separated and living in her parents’ building, a writer gives stand-up comedy a try. What happened next was not in the script.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last summer, the day my husband drove my daughter to sleepaway camp, I moved into my parents’ apartment building. Neighbors who had known me since childhood saw me in the elevator and asked what I was doing there. “House-sitting,” I said. In truth I was getting divorced, and crashing to save money until I found a new place for my daughter, 14, and me. When I told friends my situation, they said, “You’re the real-life Mrs. Maisel.” Minus the costuming and time period, there were striking similarities: difficult split, close Jewish family, prying neighbors. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image