l': 'By Elizabeth Williamson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williamson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62fec45b-2dd6-55a7-a895-bf73696eeedd', 'word_count': 1687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62fec45b-2dd6-55a7-a895-bf73696eeedd'}, {'abstract': 'Polio left her in a wheelchair. It also started her on a lifelong fight to change perceptions and break down real-world obstacles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/01/health/marilyn-saviola-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Polio left her in a wheelchair. It also started her on a lifelong fight to change perceptions and break down real-world obstacles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marilyn E. Saviola, who after childhood polio left her a quadriplegic spent much of her adult life advocating for people with disabilities, pushing for the removal of both the physical barriers and the attitudes that hinder people like her from fully participating in society, died on Nov. 23 at her home in Brooklyn. She was 74.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/obituaries/02saviola/merlin_11659529_abcde084-d434-49b6-b871-cb0caf2f5d21-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/02/obituaries/02saviola/merlin_11659529_abcde084-d434-49b6-b871-cb0caf2f5d21-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/obituaries/02saviola/merlin_11659529_abcde084-d434-49b6-b871-cb0caf2f5d21-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None