ame': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c9908aa-df0b-50ce-bca2-09500cbfea37', 'word_count': 2491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c9908aa-df0b-50ce-bca2-09500cbfea37'}, {'abstract': 'Armed with historical documents and a deep well of knowledge of local design, Laura Sartori Rimini and Roberto Peregalli rehabilitated a 19th-century house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2019/12/02/t-magazine/inside-studio-peregallis-meticulously-restored-swiss-home.html', 'snippet': 'Armed with historical documents and a deep well of knowledge of local design, Laura Sartori Rimini and Roberto Peregalli rehabilitated a 19th-century house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Armed with historical documents and a deep well of knowledge of local design, Laura Sartori Rimini and Roberto Peregalli rehabilitated a 19th-century house.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 760}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 808, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1616, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I/02tmag-peregalli-slide-SI8I-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Studio Peregalli’s Meticulously Restored Swiss Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-02T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4e4b3802-2ff2-5932-8ecf-085d993863ee', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4e4b3802-2ff2-5932-8ecf-085d993863ee'}, {'abstract': 'The Milanese firm Studio Peregalli has tapped into the soul of a 19th-century house in order to return it to an idealized version of its former glory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/02/t-magazine/swiss-home-studio-peregalli.html', 'snippet': 'The Milanese firm Studio Peregalli has tapped into the soul of a 19th-century house in order to return it to an idealized version of its former glory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE ITALIAN WORD patinare is often invoked at Studio Peregalli, the Milanese interior design and architecture firm co-founded by Laura Sartori Rimini and Roberto Peregalli 27 years ago. The term, which translates to “patinate,” is rarely used as a verb in English, generally because it’s something that’s accomplished by time, not by human interference. Yet the dozens of craftsmen trained and employed at the firm are able to create the illusion of age where none exists: scraping, scratching, staining, waxing or soiling walls, floors, furniture and fabrics until each element of each room looks like it’s been around for decades, if not centuries, even though it may in fact be newly reconfigured. Virtually everything that makes it into one of Studio Peregalli’s spaces that’s not already an antique undergoes this process, creating a singular aesthetic that has attracted admirers such as the late French fashion executive Pierre Bergé (the former partner of Yves Saint Laurent), the husband-and-wife American artists John Currin and Rachel Feinstein and the German publisher and philanthropist Hubert Burda.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2030, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/02/t-magazine/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-copy/02tmag-peregalli-slide-QZH4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Charming Swiss Home That Respects, and Reimagines, the Past', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studio Peregalli', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-02T10:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_des