 shows in communities all around New York City, have proved what they know how to do better than anyone else. It’s not creating a dynamic dialogue between the works onstage and the audience, although they’re wizards at it. It’s not making Shakespeare feel urgent and fresh by turning the plays on their head, although I can’t think of any other company that has made me want to sit through “The Tempest” twice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/00measure/merlin_164852217_8e09be25-5b9c-4986-bd48-7375489420b4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/00measure/merlin_164852217_8e09be25-5b9c-4986-bd48-7375489420b4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/00measure/merlin_164852217_8e09be25-5b9c-4986-bd48-7375489420b4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/00measure/merlin_164852217_8e09be25-5b9c-4986-bd48-7375489420b4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/00measure/merlin_164852217_8e09be25-5b9c-4986-bd48-7375489420b4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/00measure/merlin_164852217_8e09be25-5b9c-4986-bd48-7375489420b4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cred