: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c23e0fb-4b11-5a26-be0f-34b8d141886a', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c23e0fb-4b11-5a26-be0f-34b8d141886a'}, {'abstract': 'Stick with us here — consider the next few weeks a dry run for a habit you’ll start the New Year fully engaged with.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/02/smarter-living/new-years-resolutions.html', 'snippet': 'Stick with us here — consider the next few weeks a dry run for a habit you’ll start the New Year fully engaged with.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Year’s resolutions seem like a great way to take stock of the last year and set goals for the next one. Unfortunately, by February around 80 percent of people have failed to stick to theirs. Life-changing commitments are just hard to, well, commit to. If most people can’t stay at it for six weeks, something must be wrong with the whole process.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/00sl_resolutions/00sl_resolutions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/00sl_resolutions/00sl_resolutions-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/00sl_resolutions/00sl_resolutions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/00sl_resolutions/00sl_resolutions-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/00sl_resolutions/00sl_resolutions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/00sl_resolutions/00sl_resolutions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/00sl_resolutions/00sl_resolutions-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Should Start Practicing New Year’s Resolutions Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Start Living Your New Year’s Resolutions Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-02T22:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Smarter Living', 'section_name': 'Smarter Living', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harry Guinness', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Guinness', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3c41d84-b79a-566c-8fe3-395d6fbc4647', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3c41d84-b79a-566c-8fe3-395d6fbc4647'}, {'abstract': 'At Harvard’s Peabody Museum, a new exhibition explores American social history through food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/02/dining/food-social-history-peabody.html', 'snippet': 'At Harvard’s Peabody Museum, a new exhibition explores American social history through food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1910, a group of Harvard freshmen attended a formal dinner, sipped imported Champagne, smoked cigarettes and tasted an elaborate Eastern European “tree cake.” The privilege and wealth of these young men, who were all most likely white, can be seen from the forks and dishes they left behind around an oak dining table. This dinner is the centerpiece of Resetting the Table, an exhibition at the Peabody Museum of Archaeology & Ethnology at Harvard. Along with other food objects, the exhibition explores inclusion and exclusion in American history, as well as the social, political, economic and technological influences on the way Americans have eaten. Prehistoric oyster shells, late 20th-century Budweiser cans excavated from Harvard Yard and a life-size diorama of an early 20th-century kitchen will also be on display.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/dining/02burner1/merlin_165083121_ece1d40d-30b2-44a7-a9f1-222f9a4f8655-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/04/dining/02burner1/merlin_165083121_ece1d40d-30b2-44a7-a9f1-222f9a4f8655-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/dining/02burner1/merlin_165083121_ece1d40d-30b2-44a7-a9f1-222f9a4f8655-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/dining/02burner1/merlin_165083121_ece1d40d-30b2-44a7-a9f1-222f9a4f8655-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1281, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/dining/02burner1/02burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/04/dining/02burner1/02burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/dining/02burner1/02burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Meal Caught in Time', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Study: A Meal From 1910 Caught in Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peabody Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambridge (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-02T22:47:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amelia Nierenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amelia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nierenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0170158-bac6-55a3-896d-7243458b95a7', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0170158-bac6-55a3-896d-7243458b95a7'}, {'abstract': 'The appointment would pit the governor against President Trump, revealing an intraparty rift over the best way to maintain Republican dominance in Georgia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/02/us/loeffler-kemp-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The appointment would pit the governor against President Trump, revealing an intraparty r