 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/532cae6b-7e44-57d3-8c63-0e620d862405', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/532cae6b-7e44-57d3-8c63-0e620d862405'}, {'abstract': 'In the stellar “And Still You Must Swing” at the Joyce Theater, she is joined by Jason Samuels Smith, Derick K. Grant and Camille A. Brown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/04/arts/dance/dormeshia-and-still-you-must-swing-review.html', 'snippet': 'In the stellar “And Still You Must Swing” at the Joyce Theater, she is joined by Jason Samuels Smith, Derick K. Grant and Camille A. Brown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dance relies on technique, but if that’s all there is, a performance loses its dimension; its energy fizzles out. There are many points to be made about an excellent show like “And Still You Must Swing,” led by Dormeshia, a tap dancer of exceptional elegance, dazzling speed and, yes, an abundance of technique. But above all, at its foundation, there is heart and conviction. And, mission accomplished: It swings. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/04dormeshia-2/merlin_165386700_eac9c86b-542b-43d4-b5ef-7cba354abcbd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/04dormeshia-2/merlin_165386700_eac9c86b-542b-43d4-b5ef-7cba354abcbd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/04dormeshia-2/merlin_165386700_eac9c86b-542b-43d4-b5ef-7cba354abcbd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/arts/04dormeshia-2/merlin_165386700_eac