o unchecked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/04/opinion/kamala-harris-black-women.html', 'snippet': 'Kamala Harris’s campaign had its flaws, but we can’t let liberal biases go unchecked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Senator Kamala Harris of California entered the race for the Democratic presidential nomination in January, many believed she would be hard to beat. Telegenic, highly educated and from a multiethnic background, she would have been an ideal candidate in the pre-Obama era. We expected her to create an All-American narrative that is relatable to a wide cross-section of the country; that’s how President Barack Obama ascended in 2004. But Ms. Harris failed to do that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/opinion/04Price/merlin_157871094_9cf1d4f0-9138-4a0e-bdd6-3906fd82d5f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/04/opinion/04Price/merlin_157871094_9cf1d4f0-9138-4a0e-bdd6-3906fd82d5f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/opinion/04Price/merlin_157871094_9cf1d4f0-9138-4a0e-bdd6-3906fd82d5f8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/opinion/04Price/merlin_157871094_9cf1d4f0-9138-4a0e-bdd6-3906fd82d5f8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/opinion/04Price/04Price-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda