tional Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pompeo, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hale, David Maclain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamdok, Abdalla', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-05T00:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac87334c-c258-5708-91b1-795413c51fa7', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac87334c-c258-5708-91b1-795413c51fa7'}, {'abstract': 'Residents in the nation’s slums suffer with the economy’s collapse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/04/opinion/venezuela-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'Residents in the nation’s slums suffer with the economy’s collapse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To visit Venezuela today is to see how misrule can shatter a country. Years of corrupt, incompetent and autocratic rule have left Venezuelans hungry and children dying for want of basic medical care. Daniela Serrano, above, lost a child this year to malnutrition and now watches apprehensively as her daughter, Daryelis, 3, undergoes a health exam at a clinic affiliated with an aid group, Proyecto Nodriza. Some Venezuelans fear that famine lies ahead, and it seems easier to find supporters of President Nicolás Maduro on an American university campus than in Venezuela itself. Words can’t capture the misery, so I’m giving my column space over to photos of people I met on a recent visit. People were willing to be photographed and share their stories so that the world could understand what their country is enduring.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/04kristof1/merlin_164812473_8d7e788a-9f7a-4a61-a5f3-94c26f2d3464-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/04kristof1/merlin_164812473_8d7e788a-9f7a-4a61-a5f3-94c26f2d3464-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/04kristof1/merlin_164812473_8d7e788a-9f7a-4a61-a5f3-94c26f2d3464-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/04kristof1/merlin_164812473_8d7e788a-9f7a-4a61-a5f3-94c26f2d3464-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/04kristof1/05kristof1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/04kristof1/05kristof1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/04kristof1/05kristof1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width