 a director at the Bird Genoscape Project, which oversees a collection of more than 200,000 bird feathers used by scientists to extract genetic material and better understand where birds go, what makes them vulnerable and how they might survive a changing climate. Nearly a third of all North American birds, some three billion, have vanished since 1970, and biologists are calling for urgent action to avoid “future avifaunal collapse.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08Mag-Tip-1/08Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08Mag-Tip-1/08Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 544}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08Mag-Tip-1/08Mag-Tip-1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08Mag-Tip-1/08Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08Mag-Tip-1/08Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08Mag-Tip-1/08Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08Mag-Tip-1/08Mag-Tip-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'sub