graph': 'A poem can hold mysteries more easily than any factual timeline. In a rush of breath and syllables, someone lives and departs, is gone without being gone, diminished then departed, but reappearing always, unexpectedly, in indelible ways. In “pray me stay eager,” the collection in which this poem appears, Ellen Doré Watson is a master of the spontaneous moment, the merging and blending of consciousness, the delicious difficulties of relationships and questions rising from an intensified experience. Selected by Naomi Shihab Nye', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-jumbo-v3.png', 'height': 134, 'width': 386, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 134, 'width': 386, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Mother Going Gone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-05T10:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Doré Watson and Naomi Shihab Nye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': 'Doré', 'lastname': 'Watson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Shihab', 'lastname': 'Nye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4217a09a-cfbb-5e22-8562-88ffc0d9edb5', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4217a09a-cfbb-5e22-8562-88ffc0d9edb5'}, {'abstract': 'As the head of a $185 billion technology company, Chuck Robbins says, “We have to run a good business, but there’s more to it.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/05/business/chuck-robbins-cisco-corner-office.html', 'snippet': 'As the head of a $185 billion technology company, Chuck Robbins says, “We have to run a good business, but there’s more to it.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Business Roundtable issued a statement in August arguing that companies should no longer advance only the interests of shareholders, Cisco’s chief executive, Chuck Robbins, was among those acclaiming the release as a seminal moment for corporate America. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/business/05CORNEROFFICE-01/05CORNEROFFICE-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/08/business/05CORNEROFFICE-01/05CORNEROFFICE-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/business/05CORNEROFFICE-01/05CORNE