657c9'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s chief classical music critic and a loyal reader (and listener) wrestle with the boundaries of programming.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/06/arts/music/philharmonic-critic.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s chief classical music critic and a loyal reader (and listener) wrestle with the boundaries of programming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Anthony Tommasini faulted the conductor Philippe Jordan in a review for leading a program of repertory staples — including Beethoven’s Seventh Symphony — with the New York Philharmonic in late October, a reader wrote Mr. Tommasini an email with his vehement disagreement. It led to a lively exchange between the two about what classical music audiences really want. The following correspondence has been edited and condensed.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/08the-playback/merlin_163607877_249bc079-d0c4-4cbb-bfc8-91263dc24461-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/08the-playback/merlin_163607877_249bc079-d0c4-4cbb-bfc8-91263dc24461-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/08the-playback/merlin_163607877_249bc079-d0c4-4cbb-bfc8-91263dc24461-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/08the-playback/merlin_163607877_249bc079-d0c4-4cbb-bfc8-91263dc24461-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'c