ared in print on Monday, Dec. 9, 2019.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Corrections: Dec. 9, 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-09T05:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbffdfd0-5365-56aa-ad5e-04c0572367e0', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbffdfd0-5365-56aa-ad5e-04c0572367e0'}, {'abstract': 'Etiquette helps you get on in life, but having a range of etiquette makes all the difference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/09/smarter-living/digital-etiquette-manners-online.html', 'snippet': 'Etiquette helps you get on in life, but having a range of etiquette makes all the difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have made many a digital etiquette faux pas in my time. I used to be that person in the office who always replied to a group email first to show how keen I was, but really I was just coming across as annoying and needy. I spammed my social media with MySpace-angle selfies — camera held aloft, lips pouting like a fish — in my formative online years. I have even ghosted someone.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/smarter-living/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo/09sl-digitalhandshake-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Live Your Life Online. Don’t Forget Your Manners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Ensure A Good Impression', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-09T05:38:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Smarter Living', 'section_name': 'Smarter Living', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Turk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23bd74fe-dab4-50dd-9a5c-b85371bed573', 'word_count': 1441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23bd74fe-dab4-50dd-9a5c-b85371bed573'}, {'abstract': 'The extended cut of the wedding comedy arrives on HBO. And Trey Edward Shults’s horror movie jumps from Amazon to Netflix.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/09/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday-bridesmaids-and-it-comes-at-night.html', 'snippet': 'The extended cut of the wedding comedy arrives on HBO. And Trey Edward Shults’s horror movie jumps from Amazon to Netflix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRIDESMAIDS (EXTENDED VERSION) (2011) Stream on HBO. Rent on Amazon, Google Play, iTunes, Vudu and YouTube. Paul Feig directs as Kristen Wiig stars as Annie, the disastrous maid of honor for the wedding of her lifelong friend Lillian (Maya Rudolph). The movie, written by Wiig and Annie Mumolo, follows the chaotic gaggle of bridesmaids through the ups and downs of matrimonial rites of passage — dress fittings, bachelorette parties, bridal showers — and twists each ritual into a new catastrophe. As Manohla Dargis wrote of “Bridesmaids” in her Times review, “Ms. Wiig and Ms. Mumolo want to make you giggle and snort — but they get at the layers of insanity in weddings as well as the joys.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/arts/09TVcol-Bridesmaids/bridesmaids-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/09/arts/09TVcol-Bridesmaids/bridesmaids-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/arts/09TVcol-Bridesmaids/bridesmaids-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/arts/09TVcol-Bridesmaids/bridesmaids-span-thumbStandard.j