one, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d043a2b3-374c-521d-bf1e-2ebfc79d3f71', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d043a2b3-374c-521d-bf1e-2ebfc79d3f71'}, {'abstract': 'A last-minute booking, a furtive cab ride and a spy in the window. How our correspondent found a crack in China’s surveillance state — and a woman on her deathbed in Xinjiang.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/09/podcasts/the-daily/a-womans-journey-through-chinas-detention-camps.html', 'snippet': 'A last-minute booking, a furtive cab ride and a spy in the window. How our correspondent found a crack in China’s surveillance state — and a woman on her deathbed in Xinjiang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listen and subscribe to our podcast from your mobile device: Via Apple Podcasts | Via RadioPublic | Via Stitcher', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Woman’s Journey Through China’s Detention Camps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Facial Recognition Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-09T11:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'subsection_name': 'The Daily', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/171eb057-031c-583a-9bc7-fdaf0812eb5b', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/171eb057-031c-583a-9bc7-fdaf0812eb5b'}, {'abstract': 'The world is failing innocent victims of the war on terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/09/opinion/isis-children.html', 'snippet': 'The world is failing innocent victims of the war on terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children peer out from behind the bars into the light, scarred by intense trauma and uncertain of their future, terrified both of their prison and the outside world. The images and stories of these youngsters, robbed of their childhood by the extreme violence of life under the Islamic State, are harrowing. Many are unaccompanied, the large majority are under 12. They now find themselves abandoned in appalling conditions in rudimentary camps in Syria. Governments have to do better: This is not the way to treat children who are also victims of terrorism. Nor is it effective counterterrorism policy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/opinion/09gilmour/merlin_152756337_baca6ccb-5a35-449c-88c2-c4cede1ae52c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/09/opinion/09gilmour/merlin_152756337_baca6ccb-5a35-449c-88c2-c4cede1ae52c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/opinion/09gilmour/merlin_152756337_baca6ccb-5a35-449c-88c2-c4cede1ae52c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/09/opinion/09gilmour/merlin_152756337_baca6ccb-5a35-449c-88c2-c4cede1ae52c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0