e skyrocketed and people flocked east in search of affordable homes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEAUMONT, Calif. — When Lynn Baldi moved to Beaumont in 1978, the Riverside County city was mostly shrub land, apple orchards and empty lots. That open space was exactly what she wanted. Ms. Baldi, now 72, had been living in San Bernardino and was looking for a quieter place to raise her children. At the time, Beaumont — now one of the most rapidly growing cities in California — was sleepy and pastoral. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/10/realestate/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/10/realestate/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/10/realestate/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/10/realestate/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/10/realestate/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/10/realestate/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL/10Living-CA-Baumont-slide-96BL-thumbStandard.j