t', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frontier Airlines Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-10T20:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Galen Sherwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Galen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sherwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/806b99a3-d939-560e-807f-eae82148e0e0', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806b99a3-d939-560e-807f-eae82148e0e0'}, {'abstract': 'At the new Cirque Mechanics show, the revolving ring, rotating ladders and spinning swings might not thrill, but the performers do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/10/theater/42-ft-circus-review.html', 'snippet': 'At the new Cirque Mechanics show, the revolving ring, rotating ladders and spinning swings might not thrill, but the performers do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nice thing about a circus is that it wants you to be happy. Others shows challenge you, provoke you, make you think, make you feel. But a bigtop-style spectacle aims directly for your pleasure receptors, offering a dose of dopamine, cut with adrenaline and delivered straight to your seat. Or isn’t that what everyone experiences when Battulga Battogtokh, a strongman from Mongolia, hefts three women simultaneously?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/10/arts/1042ft-2/merlin_165457668_6eb5e02d-6e67-4c24-b652-daf1a44a437e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/10/arts/1042ft-2/merlin_165457668_6eb5e02d-6e67-4c24-b652-daf1a44a437e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, '