': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, December 11, 2019.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It cut out the sun, it went dark. You couldn’t see that there was an island there. It was completely covered in ash.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Eruption Forces New Zealand to Rethink Its Tolerance for Risk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-11T03:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/41ba0c05-fb4f-5510-a48e-eb3d86910968', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41ba0c05-fb4f-5510-a48e-eb3d86910968'}, {'abstract': 'President Trump told supporters at a Pennsylvania rally that they were “lucky I became your president” before denouncing the impeachment effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/10/us/politics/trump-impeachment-rally-pennsylvania.html', 'snippet': 'President Trump told supporters at a Pennsylvania rally that they were “lucky I became your president” before denouncing the impeachment effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HERSHEY, Pa. — President Trump told supporters on Tuesday at a rally in Pennsylvania that they were “lucky I became your president” before entering into a screed against House Democrats for introducing articles of impeachment against him, calling the effort “flimsy” and “the lightest impeachment in the history of our country.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/10/business/10dc-trump1/merlin_165764526_26cce3a9-5c8e-4c52-9acf-cc9ff7f9c01b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': '