/74b5e4a8-6dbc-5b76-8d4d-fda69222d1be', 'word_count': 1427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74b5e4a8-6dbc-5b76-8d4d-fda69222d1be'}, {'abstract': 'It comes down to decisions made by two men half a century ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/11/magazine/birth-control-pill-period.html', 'snippet': 'It comes down to decisions made by two men half a century ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1960s, manufacturers of the new birth-control pill imagined their ideal user as feminine, maternal and forgetful. She wanted discretion. She was married. And she wanted visible proof that her monthly cycle was normal and that she wasn’t pregnant.', 'print_section': 'SS', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility-03/mag-fertility-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility-03/mag-fertility-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility-03/mag-fertility-03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility-03/mag-fertility-03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility-03/mag-fertility-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility-03/mag-fertility-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility-03/mag-fertility-03-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Women on the Pill Still ‘Need’ to Have Their Periods', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Origin of the Fake Period', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menstruation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ROCK, JOHN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagner, David P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-11T15:05:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel E. Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/748716ad-7236-5deb-9438-872b4be39ab3', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/748716ad-7236-5deb-9438-872b4be39ab3'}, {'abstract': 'Most women never use their frozen eggs to become pregnant. But that’s not necessarily the point.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/11/magazine/egg-freezing-fertility.html', 'snippet': 'Most women never use their frozen eggs to become pregnant. But that’s not necessarily the point.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, egg-freezing seems like an ideal technological solution to a longstanding human conundrum: What if women could postpone having children to the exact time in their lives that made the most sense for them? And the rising popularity of egg-freezing and the easy-breezy marketing surrounding it — “egg-freezing for the price of a healthy snack,” according to one ad featuring açaí berries and a smiling cartoon egg — make it seem as if the prospects of having a child were essentially a given.', 'print_section': 'SS', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility/mag-fertility-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility/mag-fertility-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility/mag-fertility-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility/mag-fertility-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility/mag-fertility-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility/mag-fertility-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/03/magazine/mag-fertility/mag-fertility-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unexpected Freedom That Comes With Freezing Your Eggs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unexpected Options', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egg Donation and Freezing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IVF Guide LLC (FertilityIQ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARTIFICIAL INSEMINATION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-11T15:07:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Lampert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lampert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23e7cf92-bf70-5042-99e4-fdb6cf3bd221', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23e7cf92-bf70-5042-99e4-fdb6cf3bd221'}, {'abstract': 'It’s easier than ever to find out who your biological parents are. But when deception is uncovered, there aren’t many laws to help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/11/magazine/fertility-fraud-sperm.html', 'snippet': 'It’s easier than ever to find out who your biological parents are. But when deception is uncovered, there aren’t many laws to help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scores of families, using commercial DNA testing kits, have learned in recent years that, decades ago, their doctors lied to them. The doctors told infertile couples seeking artificial insemination that they would use sperm from a medical student, from someone who resembled the husband or simply from an anonymous donor. Instead, the doctors used their own sperm — a disturbing and profound violation of medical ethics. It’s called fertility fraud. But is it unlawful?', 'print_section': 'SS', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/magazine/mag-fertitiltyfraud/mag-fertitiltyfraud-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/04/magazine/mag-fertitiltyfraud/mag-fertitiltyfraud-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/magazine/mag-fertitiltyfraud/mag-fertitiltyfraud-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/magazine/mag-fertitiltyfraud/mag-fertitiltyfraud-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1446, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/magazine/mag-fertitiltyfraud/mag-fertitiltyfraud-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/04/magazine/mag-fertitiltyfraud/mag-fertitiltyfraud-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/04/magazine/mag-fertitiltyfraud/mag-fertitiltyfraud-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Dad Turns Out to Be the Fertility Doctor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fighting Fertility Fraud', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertil