mate, pursued the terrorist and sprayed him with a fire extinguisher, slowing his advance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A woman’s scream was the first sign John Crilly had of a terrorist attack. For a moment, he wasn’t sure it signaled real distress, he said, but then “it got a lot louder, a lot more intense.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/world/12london1/merlin_165328974_f02a4d60-9881-4b0e-ab4a-72386dfe9686-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/12/world/12london1/merlin_165328974_f02a4d60-9881-4b0e-ab4a-72386dfe9686-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/world/12london1/merlin_165328974_f02a4d60-9881-4b0e-ab4a-72386dfe9686-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/world/12london1/merlin_165328974_f02a4d60-9881-4b0e-ab4a-72386dfe9686-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/world/12london1/12london1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/12/world/12london1/12london1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/world/12london1/12london1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Subduing Terrorist on London Bridge, He Was Prepared to Die', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' In Chasing London Attacker, He Was Braced to Lose His Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cambridge University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Saskia (d 2019)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Usman (d 2019)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merritt, Jack (d 2019)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-12T16:47:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Iliana Magra', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Iliana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Magra', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45b6cb5c-f7b6-5142-8d66-4ad976c2468a', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45b6cb5c-f7b6-5142-8d66-4ad976c2468a'}, {'abstract': 'Jews aren’t a race. But anti-Semitism can be racism for legal purposes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/12/opinion/trumps-executive-order-has-firm-legal-grounding.html', 'snippet': 'Jews aren’t a race. But anti-Semitism can be racism for legal purposes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump signed an executive order on Wednesday instructing federal agencies to use Title VI — the law that bars federally funded programs from discriminating on the basis of “race, color, or national origin” — to combat anti-Semitism. That move sparked uproar from critics who stressed that Jews are not a race or nationality and argued that it confirmed “centuries-old anti-Semitic tropes.” But Mr. Trump’s interpretation of Title VI as applying to anti-Semitism is neither new nor troubling. The characterization of anti-Semitism as a form of racial or national-origin discrimination has a secure place in American law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/opinion/12Hemel/merlin_165814917_f7cb6477-9c66-417f-a4fe-6fdb038a7fcf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/12/opinion/12Hemel/merlin_165814917_f7cb6477-9c66-417f-a4fe-6fdb038a7fcf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/opinion/12Hemel/merlin_165814917_f7cb6477-9c66-417f-a4fe-6fdb038a7fcf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/opinion/12Hemel/merlin_165814917_f7cb6477-9c66-417f-a4fe-6fdb038a7fcf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/opinion/12Hemel/12Hemel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/12/opinion/12Hemel/12Hemel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype