'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/12/health/fda-stephen-hahn.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration has been without a permanent commissioner since April, when Dr. Scott Gottlieb resigned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate voted 72 to 18 to confirm Dr. Stephen Hahn as commissioner of the Food and Drug Administration, as the agency faces pressure to reduce teenage vaping and weighs competing interests on a long-delayed proposal to ban flavored e-cigarettes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/science/12FDA/12FDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/12/science/12FDA/12FDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/science/12FDA/12FDA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/science/12FDA/12FDA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/science/12FDA/12FDA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/12/science/12FDA/12FDA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/12/science/12FDA/12FDA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Confirms Stephen Hahn to Head F.D.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vote Confirms Trump’s Pick For the F.D.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Cigarettes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MD Anderson Cancer Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hahn, Stephen M (1960- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-healthcare', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-12T19:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7432d199-bee5-5733-b56d-f384d3a3540d', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7432d199-bee5-5733-b56d-f384d3a3540d'}, {'abstract': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/12/books/review/11-new-books-we-recommend-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most weeks we hew to a pretty traditional notion of “books” around here: text-based narratives printed on paper and bound between covers, with occasional swerves to accommodate our love of poetry and audiobooks and graphic novels and what have you. But in a world where Bob Dylan can win the Nobel Prize for literature (I approve!), sometimes we have to let our hair down and just bask in the astonishing variety of the book world. This week our recommended titles include two different letter collections — one by the great Ralph Ellison, the other by a group of writers detailing a famous literary scandal as it unfolded in real time — along with a coffee-table book that collects images of the human body, a close look at popular tunes from the American songbook, a meditation on Italian painting, and a poet’s essayistic reflections on the sources and significance of tears. Not a plain old novel or buttoned-up narrative to be found in that group.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/books/15edchoice1/15edchoice1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 301, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/15/books/15edchoice1/15edchoice1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 301}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/books/15edchoice1/15edchoice1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/books/15edchoice1/15edchoice1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 2027, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/books/15edchoice1/15edchoice1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/15/books/15edchoice1/15edchoice1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/books/15edchoice1/15edchoice1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '11 New Books We Recommend This Week', 'kicker': 'Editors’ Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice / Staff Picks From the Book Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-12T19:43:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8a6f4d3-4057-5f2c-8e5b-ed1e89a02aa4', 'word_count': 1367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8a6f4d3-4057-5f2c-8e5b-ed1e89a02aa4'}, {'abstract': 'Teenage comments in response to our recent writing prompts, and an invitation to join the ongoing conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/12/learning/what-students-are-saying-about-reparations-what-they-want-to-learn-in-school-and-individuality.html', 'snippet': 'Teenage comments in response to our recent writing prompts, and an invitation to join the ongoing conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s roundup of student comments on our writing prompts, we asked young people to weigh in on whether the United States owes reparations to the descendants of slaves, tell us what they wished they could learn in school, and reflect on their identities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/26/business/23reparations3-LN/23reparations3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/26/business/23reparations3-LN