:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Benner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59bebbb4-13fe-5a22-a419-989198726638', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59bebbb4-13fe-5a22-a419-989198726638'}, {'abstract': 'He was over 70. I was 22. We both loved Fran Lebowitz. What was I doing on the back of his motorcycle?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/13/style/modern-love-it-wasnt-me-he-wanted.html', 'snippet': 'He was over 70. I was 22. We both loved Fran Lebowitz. What was I doing on the back of his motorcycle?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Running my hands down my jeans as I waited for a drink, I thought, “Can a 22-year-old even be underdressed?” In my corduroy blazer and dark-washed jeans, I was the youngest person in this Boston theater by a generation, the seemingly lone millennial delegate for an evening meet-and-greet with Fran Lebowitz before her onstage conversation. This V.I.P. access came at a higher cost, but I figured if I nixed buying almonds for a few months I could balance my budget.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/fashion/15MODERNLOVE/15MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/15/fashion/15MODERNLOVE/15MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/fashion/15MODERNLOVE/15MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'j