'uri': 'nyt://article/14d2c1e9-b11b-5fd6-977f-50526363fe22'}, {'abstract': '‘Trump anxiety disorder’ has morphed into anxiety about everything, and impeachment isn’t helping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/13/us/politics/Donald-Trump-2020.html', 'snippet': '‘Trump anxiety disorder’ has morphed into anxiety about everything, and impeachment isn’t helping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENWOOD, S.C. — The past three years have not been easy for the political fortunes or the emotional health of America’s Democrats. To the extent they feel optimistic about anything, they have been waiting for the 2020 election in the way inhabitants of a storm-ravaged city might look toward the end of hurricane season — as an opportunity to restore order not just to their fractured physical world, but to their battered psyches.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/us/politics/00anxieties1/merlin_164134509_a585e648-f474-4fb3-bd99-c0840c97ffd5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/28/us/politics/00anxieties1/merlin_164134509_a585e648-f474-4fb3-bd99-c0840c97ffd5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/us/politics/00anxieties1/merlin_164134509_a585e648-f474-4fb3-bd99-c0840c97ffd5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/us/politics/00anxieties1/merlin_164134509_a585e648-f474-4fb3-bd99-c0840c97ffd5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/us/politics/00anxieties1/00anxieties1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/28/us/politics/00anxieties1/00anxieties1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/28/us/politics/00anxieties1/00anxieties1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Agree on One Thing: They’re Very, Very Nervous', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Impeachment and 2020 Loom, Democrats Unite in Worry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-13T10:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e67aa0ff-c445-51fb-a4f1-a5f55fc67d84', 'word_count': 1808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e67aa0ff-c445-51fb-a4f1-a5f55fc67d84'}, {'abstract': 'The “Shrill” pool party. The “David Makes Man” pilot. The quietest installment of the final “Game of Thrones” season. These are the episodes that stuck with us this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/13/arts/television/the-best-tv-episodes-of-2019.html', 'snippet': 'The “Shrill” pool party. The “David Makes Man” pilot. The quietest installment of the final “Game of Thrones” season. These are the episodes that stuck with us this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one can watch all the TV shows anymore, even a professional, and that goes a thousandfold for TV episodes. So I can’t claim these to be definitively the best installments of TV in 2019. They’re just the ones that have stuck most in my mind as we head into 2020. (For variety’s sake, I’m skipping the many terrific episodes of the shows I already put on my 10-best list, among them “Anna Ishii-Peters” from “Pen15” and the mind-blowing “This Extraordinary Being” from “Watchmen.”) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/00episodes-year-end-promo/00episodes-year-end-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/00episodes-year-end-promo/00episodes-year-end-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/00episodes-year-end-promo/00episodes-year-end-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/00episodes-year-end-promo/00episodes-year-end-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/00episodes-year-end-promo/00episodes-year-end-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/00episodes-year-end-promo/00episodes-year-end-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/08/arts/00episodes-year-end-promo/00episodes-year-end-promo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best TV Episodes of 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Just Episodes, but Standouts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Crashing (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'David Makes Man (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fosse/Verdon (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Frontline (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Game of Thrones (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gentleman Jack (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lodge 49 (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Molly of Denali (TV Program)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Pose (TV Program)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ramy (TV Program)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rick and Morty (TV Program)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Shrill (TV Program)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Unbelievable (TV Program)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-13T10:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Poniewozik, Mike Hale and Margaret Lyons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b6c63e4-d59e-57b7-9d47-9af198ec5041', 'word_count': 2013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b6c63e4-d59e-57b7-9d47-9af198ec5041'}, {'abstract': 'In a city with a sleek, squeaky-clean downtown, the lifestyle editor Sara Harowitz finds authenticity in a neighborhood that has retained its blue collar roots. She shares her favorite spots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/13/travel/five-places-to-visit-in-vancouver-sara-harowitz.html', 'snippet': 'In a city with a sleek, squeaky-clean downtown, the lifestyle editor Sara Harowitz finds authenticity in a neighborhood that has retained its blue collar roots. She shares her favorite spots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vancouver, with its snowcapped mountains and sleek, squeaky-clean downtown can seem to a new visitor to be lacking in urban grit. Which is exactly why for Sara Harowitz, a Vancouver native, the once blue-collar district of Hastings-Sunrise has so much appeal. Today, the area is a mix of on-trend eateries and boutiques as well as mainstays from its humbler days, and Ms. Harowitz loves the variety. “It’s unpolished, it’s working class, it’s a real Vancouver neighborhood,” says Ms. Harowitz, who edits the online lifestyle journal Basenotes, which explores wellness and female-centric travel, beauty and sustainability. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 's