m in front of a microphone. Kimmel says, “I always wanted to be an artist. That was my goal. I’d draw insulting caricatures of my teachers and classmates, or I’d sit in front of the television drawing David Letterman.” This month, his dream came true: Kimmel published “The Serious Goose,” a read-aloud magnet that is now No. 1 on the children’s picture books list. (It should come with a warning: “May rev kids up.”)', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/books/review/22Insidethelist_Kimmel/22Insidethelist_Kimmel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/books/review/22Insidethelist_Kimmel/22Insidethelist_Kimmel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 714}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/books/review/22Insidethelist_Kimmel/22Insidethelist_Kimmel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 861, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/books/review/22Insidethelist_Kimmel/22Insidethelist_Kimmel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1721, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/books/review/22Insidethelist_Kimmel/22Insidethelist_Kimmel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/22/books/review/22Insidethelist_Kimmel/22Insidethelist_Kimmel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,