dear God, are people still actually calling one another in today’s world? (And do you have to do that, too?)', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/10/smarter-living/10sl-emailend-promo/10sl-emailend-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/10/smarter-living/10sl-emailend-promo/10sl-emailend-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/10/smarter-living/10sl-emailend-promo/10sl-emailend-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/10/smarter-living/10sl-emailend-promo/10sl-emailend-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/10/smarter-living/10sl-emailend-promo/10sl-emailend-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/10/smarter-living/10sl-emailend-promo/10sl-emailend-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/10/smarter-living/10sl-emailend-promo/10sl-emailend-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right Way to Close Out an Email. (Skip That Inspirational Quote.)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Enhance Your Signature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-16T03:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Smarter Living', 'section_name': 'Smarter Living', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jen Doll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b046f081-bb02-5d46-98b1-c869b72119dc', 'word_count': 1683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b046f081-bb02-5d46-98b1-c869b72119dc'}, {'abstract': 'Damon Lindelof’s provocative “remix” of the beloved comic finished the season with confidence, completeness and no shortage of stylistic bravado.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/15/arts/television/watchmen-finale-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Damon Lindelof’s provocative “remix” of the beloved comic finished the season with confidence, completeness and no shortage of stylistic bravado.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first feeling after watching the finale of “Watchmen” is relief. Whew. Damon Lindelof has flown this plane through heavy turbulence — and a hailstorm of frozen squid — and landed it safely, which is no small achievement in itself. It was a crazy idea to riff around the consensus choice for the best graphic novel ever written, and to riff so boldly, too, by rewriting a new racial identity for Hooded Justice and plotting drastically new courses for characters like Silk Spectre II and Dr. Manhattan. (All without Alan Moore’s blessing, which he has given to no adaptation of the book.) It was audacious to shift focus from the Cold War and nuclear arms to white supremacy and racism, inviting intense scrutiny from all comers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/arts/15watchmen-recap/15watchmen-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/15/arts/15watchmen-recap/15watchmen-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/arts/15watchmen-recap/15watchmen-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/arts/15watchmen-recap/15watchmen-recap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/arts/15watchmen-recap/15watchmen-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/15/arts/15watchmen-recap/15watchmen-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/arts/15watchmen-recap/15watchmen-recap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Watchmen’ Season 1 Finale Recap: Worthy Adversaries', 'kicker': 'Watchmen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Watchmen (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-16T03:10:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Te