 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26dad8f8-1ae3-5b1d-9b96-8ada43d55de6', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26dad8f8-1ae3-5b1d-9b96-8ada43d55de6'}, {'abstract': 'The diplomats were expelled after they drove onto a base that houses the headquarters of the Navy’s SEAL Team 6. China’s denial of the accusations is the first official acknowledgment of the episode.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/16/world/asia/china-spies-explusion-military-base.html', 'snippet': 'The diplomats were expelled after they drove onto a base that houses the headquarters of the Navy’s SEAL Team 6. China’s denial of the accusations is the first official acknowledgment of the episode.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Chinese government denounced on Monday the United States’ secret expulsion this fall of two Chinese diplomats suspected of espionage, and asked for a reversal of the action. The expulsions appeared to be the first of Chinese diplomats suspected of spying in more than three decades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/16/us/politics/16dc-diplo1-sub/merlin_90450016_8e6a016b-eae1-4420-8b8e-0720ea10afa4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/16/us/politics/16dc-diplo1-sub/merlin_90450016_8e6a016b-eae1-4420-8b8e-0720ea10afa4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/16/us/politics/16dc-diplo1-sub/merlin_90450016_8e6a016b-eae1-4420-8b8e-0720ea10afa4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'c