Buddha baby. Not by me, but by many a stranger and friend — reliable observers. But when she starts kindergarten, she becomes, abruptly, no longer the Buddha baby. At night, she weeps and begs not to go to school. In the morning, the same. She is sad but also enraged. She kicks me for not having a banana. She punches me in the stomach for not being able to find her bumpy red ball. She says repeatedly that she is leaving to find a new family.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-angry-02/22mag-angry-02-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-angry-02/22mag-angry-02-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 611}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-angry-02/22mag-angry-02-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-angry-02/22mag-angry-02-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2011, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-angry-02/22mag-angry-02-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-angry-02/22mag-angry-02-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-angry-02/22mag-angry-02-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case of the Angry Daughter', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Case of the Angry Daughter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holmes, Sherlock (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGER (EMOTION)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-17T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rivka Galchen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rivka', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galchen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97bf300f-9f59-58fe-8aed-5193ed3c4343', 'word_count': 5704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97bf300f-9f59-58fe-8aed-5193ed3c4343'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to step in when you see a parent publicly berating a child and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/17/magazine/should-i-intervene-when-i-see-a-parent-mistreating-a-child.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to step in when you see a parent publicly berating a child and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I was rounding the corner in my neighborhood, I saw a teenage girl and her father in an argument. She appeared to be about 15 and was wearing a hoodie, with dyed hair; she generally looked the part of a rebellious, sullen teen. Walking behind him, the daughter kicked at her father’s heels. He responded by whipping around and throwing his full cup of coffee in her face. She responded with a number of expletives, but seemed unfazed and unhurt. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-ethicist/22mag-ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-ethicist/22mag-ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-ethicist/22mag-ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-ethicist/22mag-ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1148, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-ethicist/22mag-ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-ethicist/22mag-ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-ethicist/22mag-ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should I Intervene When I See a Parent Mistreating a Child?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Should I Intervene When I See a Parent Mistreating a Child?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-17T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f46b464-d930-5e2e-bce1-c274ac1f546e', 'word_count': 1475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f46b464-d930-5e2e-bce1-c274ac1f546e'}, {'abstract': 'Get close. Is the second hand moving smoothly? Does the engraved lettering look good?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/17/magazine/fake-rolex-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Get close. Is the second hand moving smoothly? Does the engraved lettering look good?', 'lead_paragraph': '“Is the second hand ticking in a herky-jerky-type motion?” asks Paul Altieri, founder of Bob’s Watches, one of the largest online retailers of used luxury watches. A twitchy second hand probably means you’re looking at a quartz-movement watch powered by a battery. Altieri specializes in Rolexes, which almost always run on automatic movement, where the motion of a wearer’s wrist winds an intricate system of tiny gears and springs, resulting in a smoother, sweeping second hand. Altieri can make out a cheap quartz fake from five feet away, but recently he has seen more almost-perfect impostors, what he calls “superfakes.” To catch these, you need a 10x magnifying glass and lots of time. “It really helps if you have a real one right next to it to compare,” he says. Would-be sellers send Altieri and his team of five inspectors about 700 used Rolexes a month. Usually fewer than 10 are fakes.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22Mag-Tip-1/22Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22Mag-Tip-1/22Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 570}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22Mag-Tip-1/22Mag-Tip-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 972, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22Mag-Tip-1/22Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1788, 'width': 1883, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22Mag-Tip-1/22Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22Mag-Tip-1/22Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22Mag-Tip-1/22Mag-Tip-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Spot a Counterfeit Watch', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Spot a Counterfeit Watch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Counterfeit Merchandise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-17T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da4fd458-6116-5b31-ba70-05aa882f711d', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da4fd458-6116-5b31-ba70-05aa882f711d'}, {'abstract': 'It makes the sublime available to the masses — what’s so bad about that?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/17/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-cheap-sushi.html', 'snippet': 'It makes the sublime available to the masses — what’s so bad about that?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For several years in the early 2000s, I made mediocre sushi at a Japanese restaurant in suburban Virginia. I never intended to take up the knife; I never thought I could. I started as a dishwasher, and when I made it into the kitchen, I mostly prepared yakitori and tempura. But then one busy night, the head sushi chef, who was also the owner — and who would sometimes sing Japanese folk songs to customers in an Orbison-esque tenor — poked his head into the kitchen and made a fateful request. “Jon!” he called. “Make sushi!”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22-mag-LOR/22-mag-LOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22-mag-LOR/22-mag-LOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22-mag-LOR/22-mag-LOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':