 on Wednesday, Dec. 18, 2019.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Monday about the resources allocated by different states for the 2020 census referred incorrectly to an online Census Bureau map related to response rates: It shows the predicted likelihood of a low response rate in 2020 for most census tracts, not the actual rate for 2010. It also misstated the total number of census tracts: There are 73,057, not 66,000. And it gave an outdated title for Ann Beeson at the Center for Public Policy Priorities: She is now chief executive, not executive director.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: Dec. 18, 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-18T04:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8487708-1cbe-5a68-b0ad-21923e18301c', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8487708-1cbe-5a68-b0ad-21923e18301c'}, {'abstract': 'The Cheops orbiter will give a closer examination to stars already known to host exoplanets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/18/science/cheops-satellite-launch.html', 'snippet': 'The Cheops orbiter will give a closer examination to stars already known to host exoplanets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Space Agency is continuing the search for new Earths this week with the launch of Cheops, a new telescope whose name stands for CHaracterising ExOPlanet Satellite.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/17/science/17CHEOPS01/merlin_165802395_a0c99003-cacd-40ba-8bb9-68f03facc0c5-articleLarge.jpg', 'heig