tion': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1bcfc83-a3e4-5c60-911a-1eee5ebae6c0', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1bcfc83-a3e4-5c60-911a-1eee5ebae6c0'}, {'abstract': 'How an internal power struggle, a New York State investigation and accusations of fraud and betrayal on all sides have left the longtime leader of the gun-rights organization reeling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/18/magazine/wayne-lapierre-nra-guns.html', 'snippet': 'How an internal power struggle, a New York State investigation and accusations of fraud and betrayal on all sides have left the longtime leader of the gun-rights organization reeling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wayne LaPierre was sitting in a chair with his hands over his ears, looking straight down. “It was horribly painful,” he said of the nearly two years of investigations, intrigue and infighting that have roiled the National Rifle Association, which he has led since 1991. Now, a once-invincible organization, and its chief, are girding for a legal reckoning. “I mean,” LaPierre said, looking up, “it’s the most painful period of my life.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-nra-images/22mag-nra-images-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-nra-images/22mag-nra-images-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 711}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag-nra-images/22mag-nra-images-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/magazine/22mag