terial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e17ff25-9e15-5d10-8a3e-1cd328686eba', 'word_count': 1651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e17ff25-9e15-5d10-8a3e-1cd328686eba'}, {'abstract': 'A Southern California native went looking for an old-fashioned Christmas. She found it in the “Christmas ornament town” of Seiffen, tucked in Germany’s Ore Mountains.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/18/travel/christmas-ornament-town-seiffen-erzgebirge-ore-mountains.html', 'snippet': 'A Southern California native went looking for an old-fashioned Christmas. She found it in the “Christmas ornament town” of Seiffen, tucked in Germany’s Ore Mountains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For as long as I can remember, I’ve had this image of Christmas: a village nestled in a snowy valley, candlelit windows glowing against a night sky. I’m not sure where it came from. Growing up in sunny Southern California, my family strung lights on the palm trees in our yard and went to the beach on Christmas Eve. Most kids know about Santa’s sleigh, but I believed he traveled on a magic speedboat.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/travel/13german-christmas14/13german-christmas14-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/travel/13german-christmas14/13german-christmas14-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/travel/13german-christmas14/13german-christmas14-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/travel/13german-christmas14/13german-christmas14-superJumbo.jpg', 'he