social justice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTIAGO, Chile — Through the strong will of our people, we peacefully recovered our democracy 30 years ago and gave birth to a new and modern republic, founded on three basic tenets: a deep commitment to democracy and the rule of law, an open and competitive market economy, and a strong determination to defeat poverty and increase equality of opportunities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/opinion/18pinera/18pinera-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/18/opinion/18pinera/18pinera-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/opinion/18pinera/18pinera-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/opinion/18pinera/18pinera-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/opinion/18pinera/18pinera-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/18/opinion/18pinera/18pinera-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/opinion/18pinera/18pinera-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sebastián Piñera: A New Opportunity for Chile’s Future', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinera, Sebastian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-18T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebastián Piñera Echenique', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebastián', 'middlename': 'Piñera', 'lastname': 'Echenique', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a8ae931-6cc3-5461-88ca-efe9ce90119a', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a8ae931-6cc3-5461-88ca-efe9ce90119a'}, {'abstract': 'Americans deserve a stronger assurance than “hope” that their Fourth Amendment rights are being respected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/18/opinion/fisa-court.html', 'snippet': 'Americans deserve a stronger assurance than “hope” that their Fourth Amendment rights are being respected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The F.B.I.’s investigation of the former Trump campaign adviser Carter Page, we can now say with assurance, was a train wreck. In his report, Justice Department Inspector General Michael Horowitz cataloged a damning list of egregious errors, omissions or misrepresentations in filings to the secretive Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court, which approved nearly a year’s worth of wiretaps on Mr. Page.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/multimedia/18Sanchez/18Sanchez-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLa