science/volcano-3d-reunion-island.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists spent days aboard a helicopter with special sensors over a volcano to develop a picture of how its insides affect its frequent eruptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Réunion, a French island in the western Indian Ocean, is a jigsaw of two massive shield volcanoes. The younger, Piton de la Fournaise or “peak of the furnace,” is a furious factory of lava, erupting every eight months on average over the last four decades.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/07/science/18TB-VOLCANO02/merlin_166134297_bc416a56-f6ad-47f3-9ebd-f558b06691ec-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/07/science/18TB-VOLCANO02/merlin_166134297_bc416a56-f6ad-47f3-9ebd-f558b06691ec-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/07/science/18TB-VOLCANO02/merlin_166134297_bc416a56-f6ad-47f3-9ebd-f558b06691ec-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/07/science/18TB-VOLCANO02/merlin_166134297_bc416a56-f6ad-47f3-9ebd-f558b06691ec-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1190, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/07/science/18TB-VOLCANO02/merlin_166134297_bc416a56-f6ad-47f3-9ebd-f558b06691ec-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/07/science/18TB-VOLCANO02/merlin_166134297_bc416