/video/4f3d588c-61f0-508e-a43f-b5b7b11dc299', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4f3d588c-61f0-508e-a43f-b5b7b11dc299'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s favored poem, “The Snake,” isn’t about immigrants. It’s about him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/18/opinion/trump-snake-poem-meaning.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s favored poem, “The Snake,” isn’t about immigrants. It’s about him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dating back to his days on the campaign trail, President Trump has often recited a poem called “The Snake,” as a warning about the dangers of welcoming refugees and immigrants into the country. In the Video Op-Ed above, I show how the parable is much more instructive when applied to Trump’s political rise. From his racist birther conspiracy theory to being forced to pay $2 million for using his charity for his own political gain, anyone paying close attention knew the kind of president he would be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/17/autossell/snakethumbnail1/snakethumbnail1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/17/autossell/snakethumbnail1/snakethumbnail1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/17/autossell/snakethumbnail1/snakethumbnail1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/17/autossell/snakethumbnail1/snakethumbnail1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/1