thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/world/19ambriefing-europe-promo/19ambriefing-europe4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/19/world/19ambriefing-europe-promo/19ambriefing-europe4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/world/19ambriefing-europe-promo/19ambriefing-europe4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Thursday Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-19T05:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Ives', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ives', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e82c659-d2e0-5825-9503-c968597e4830', 'word_count': 1522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e82c659-d2e0-5825-9503-c968597e4830'}, {'abstract': 'A dark reimagining of “A Christmas Carol” debuts on FX. And an unusual documentary is on Hulu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/19/arts/whats-on-tv-thursday-a-christmas-carol-and-cold-case-hammarskjold.html', 'snippet': 'A dark reimagining of “A Christmas Carol” debuts on FX. And an unusual documentary is on Hulu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A CHRISTMAS CAROL 7:30 p.m. on FX. Tombstones, darkness and cold all feature prominently in this bleak Charles Dickens rethink. Created for FX and BBC One by Steven Knight (best known for “Peaky Blinders”), this three-part, not-for-kids version of the Christmas staple stars Guy Pearce as Ebenezer Scrooge, who travels back to his childhood with the Ghost of Christmas Past (given eerie form here by Andy Serkis). The journey touches on some heavy subjects: sexual abuse, neglect (particularly by Scrooge’s father, played by Johnny Harris) and other cruelties. In a recent interview with The New York Times, Knight explained the reasoning behind some of the show’s more disturbing elements — like the abuse — that make for an especially troubling telling of the story. “I wanted to look at these things, not to disrupt or be shocking, but to say the things one can say now,” he said. “I am trying to make some suggestions about why Scrooge is Scrooge.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/arts/19tvcol-achristmascarol/19tvcol-achristmascarol-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/19/arts/19tvcol-achristmascarol/19tvcol-achristmascarol-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/arts/19tvcol-achristmascarol/19tvcol-achristmascarol-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/arts/19tvcol-achristmascarol/19tvcol-achristmascarol-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/arts/19tvcol-achristmascarol/19tvcol-achristmascarol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/19/arts/19tvcol-achristmascarol/19tvcol-achristmascarol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/arts/19tvcol-achristmascarol/19tvcol-achristmascarol-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday: ‘A Christmas Carol’ and ‘Cold Case Hammarskjold’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-19T06:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabe Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0eb2c0a-4e9a-55e0-ac87-417818de5947', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0eb2c0a-4e9a-55e0-ac87-417818de5947'}, {'abstract': 'In a corner of Doha’s old city, a state-of-the-art facility offers scans, surgeries and a link to a centuries-old pastime. Members of the royal family get to cut the line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/19/sports/qatar-falcon-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'In a corner of Doha’s old city, a state-of-the-art facility offers scans, surgeries and a link to a centuries-old pastime. Members of the royal family get to cut the line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOHA, Qatar — As soon as the clinic opens, the patients and their guardians begin streaming in. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'x