4-5cbe-426b-bf21-d47d75310bd5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/well/00teenidols/merlin_165932532_1c90c954-5cbe-426b-bf21-d47d75310bd5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/well/00teenidols/00teenidols-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/15/well/00teenidols/00teenidols-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/15/well/00teenidols/00teenidols-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Have You Coped With the Death of an Idol?', 'kicker': 'student opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-19T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Daniels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daniels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c02bea9-2b9a-5919-aa54-c779bc943abb', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c02bea9-2b9a-5919-aa54-c779bc943abb'}, {'abstract': 'Large in scope but small in size, the sonnet encapsulates infinitely malleable spirits within a finite frame, as we do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/19/well/live/when-in-distress-try-sonnets.html', 'snippet': 'Large in scope but small in size, the sonnet encapsulates infinitely malleable spirits within a finite frame, as we do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When in distress with cancer and its treatments, I think of Shakespeare “in disgrace with fortune and men’s eyes” and all alone lament my downcast state. I am not completely bereft, then, because his poem supports my complaint. Why are sonnets so bracing, I wonder as I launch into a neo-Shakespearean sort of pity party. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/smarter-living/00gubar_sonnets/00gubar_sonnets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/18/smarter-living/00gubar_sonnets/00gubar_sonnets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/smarter-living/00gubar_sonnets/00gubar_sonnets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/smarter-living/00gubar_sonnets/00gubar_sonnets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/smarter-living/00gubar_sonnets/00gubar_sonnets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/18/smarter-living/00gubar_sonnets/00gubar_sonnets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/18/smarter-living/00gubar_sonnets/00gubar_sonnets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When in Distress, Try Sonnets', 'kicker': 'Living With Cancer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-19T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5104a382-8e73-55b7-b656-d497b79f5c51', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5104a382-8e73-55b7-b656-d497b79f5c51'}, {'abstract': 'Why limit yourself to dogs and cats?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/19/magazine/judge-john-hodgman-on-getting-a-second-pet-in-a-small-apartment.html', 'snippet': 'Why limit yourself to dogs and cats?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kat writes: My boyfriend and I want to get a pet. A cat makes sense for our small apartment, but he is against having a litter box. He wants a dog and plans to build a “dog toilet” to allow it to use the bathroom autonomously. I think a dog is implausible, whereas a cat would be a great companion for our ferret, Banjo.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul