nail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Gluck/19Gluck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Gluck/19Gluck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Gluck/19Gluck-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Should You Blame if You Lose Your Health Care?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-19T20:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abbe R. Gluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abbe', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/45b71195-daa2-58e2-985a-e3ed959856b1', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45b71195-daa2-58e2-985a-e3ed959856b1'}, {'abstract': 'Bold public programs, available to everyone regardless of need, are political winners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/19/opinion/democrats-green-new-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Bold public programs, available to everyone regardless of need, are political winners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the diversity and number of candidates running for the Democratic presidential nomination, there has been a lot of agreement on a number of big policy ideas. All of the contenders want the government to guarantee paid parental leave. Nearly all want to significantly raise the federal minimum wage. Most support a Green New Deal to address climate change. Their agreement is notable, particularly on issues that in past contests were seen as radical.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Covert/19Covert-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Covert/19Covert-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 928}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Covert/19Covert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 662, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Covert/19Covert-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1324, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Covert/19Covert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Covert/19Covert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/19/opinion/19Covert/19Covert-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Americans Love Social Security', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why We Love Social Security', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-19T20:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryce Covert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Covert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a3b7403-4de5-59da-9408-6a7c982b5161', 'word_count': 971, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a3b7403-4de5-59da-9408-6a7c982b5161'}, {'abstract': 'With the future of the law in limbo, we asked them to explain what might happen now that an appeals court has sent the case back to a lower court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/19/health/obamacare-court.html', 'snippet': 'With the future of the law in limbo, we asked them to explain what might happen now that an appeals court has sent the case back to a lower court.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Ever since Judge Reed O’Connor of the Northern District of Texas ruled a year ago that the Affordable Care Act was unconstitutional, the country has been waiting for the n