: 'Delkic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6764b26-f9ad-58cf-9d46-707d18562bd4', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6764b26-f9ad-58cf-9d46-707d18562bd4'}, {'abstract': 'The season sparkles at seven holiday light displays across New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/19/arts/design/holiday-lights-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The season sparkles at seven holiday light displays across New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': ' April may be the cruelest month, but December, the darkest, can feel unkind, too. New York, however, offers its own illumination during these long, blustery nights, and not just Rockefeller Center’s seasonal sparkle. Here’s a guide to some of the lavish light displays across the city, including twinkling and towering sculptures, Chinese-style lantern shows and giant menorahs. You will usually find food, entertainment and family activities here, as well as glowing LED artifice: fairy palaces, alluring sweets, roaring dinosaurs — and lots of pandas.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Nights, Merry and Bright', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holiday Nights, Merry and Bright', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hanukkah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookfield Place (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Field (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or