: 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buttigieg, Pete (1982- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klobuchar, Amy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yang, Andrew (1975- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steyer, Thomas F', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-20T05:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e06b00a-8a10-57f5-ac76-a1552c153938', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e06b00a-8a10-57f5-ac76-a1552c153938'}, {'abstract': 'Authoritarian and divisive polices of the Modi government have pushed Indians across the country to the streets in protest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/20/opinion/india-citizenship-law-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Authoritarian and divisive polices of the Modi government have pushed Indians across the country to the streets in protest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Prime Minister Narendra Modi of India and his Hindu nationalist Bharatiya Janata Party government have deployed propaganda very successfully since coming to power in 2014. So much so that numerous egregious decisions the government has made — demonetization, electoral bonds allowing secret donations to political parties, a flawed citizens registry in the state of Assam, revoking the autonomy of Jammu and Kashmir — were accepted by a majority of people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Mody/merlin_166182366_89626dd0-1780-46e2-bae7-3bf7ceb3f42b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Mody/merlin_166182366_89626dd0-1780-46e2-bae7-3bf7ceb3f42b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Mody/merlin_166182366_89626dd0-1780-46e2-bae7-3bf7ceb3f42b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Mody/merlin_166182366_89626dd0-1780-46e2-bae7-3bf7ceb3f42b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Mody/20Mody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Mody/20Mody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Mody/20Mody-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'India Awakens to Fight for Its Soul', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shah, Amit (1964- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-20T06:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anjali Mody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anjali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf5affab-5198-5a56-b1ef-37ecc7950a2b', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf5affab-5198-5a56-b1ef-37ecc7950a2b'}, {'abstract': 'The British party’s collapse in its heartlands goes back much further than last week’s election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/20/opinion/uk-election-labour.html', 'snippet': 'The British party’s collapse in its heartlands goes back much further than last week’s election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWCASTLE UPON TYNE, England — The Labour Party’s resounding defeat in last week’s general election was not quite unexpected. But the sheer scale of the party’s collapse — especially in its postindustrial heartland areas — took many people by surprise. For large portions of the electorate, Labour’s offer was found badly wanting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Niven1/merlin_164002404_7374fc37-c4d8-44d8-9777-a85eb441fac6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Niven1/merlin_164002404_7374fc37-c4d8-44d8-9777-a85eb441fac6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 884}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Niven1/merlin_164002404_7374fc37-c4d8-44d8-9777-a85eb441fac6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 696, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Niven1/merlin_164002404_7374fc37-c4d8-44d8-9777-a85eb441fac6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Niven1/20Niven1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Niven1/20Niven1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/opinion/20Niven1/20Niven1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Labour Party’s Spectacular Defeat Had Been Coming for Decades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbyn, Jeremy (1949- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-20T06:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Niven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Niven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/41c27985-7e55-52ca-bb67-457efb767808', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41c27985-7e55-52ca-bb67-457efb767808'}, {'abstract': 'A new drama with Anthony Hopkins and Jonathan Pryce is now on Netflix. On Amazon? An adventure movie with Felicity Jones and Eddie Redmayne.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/20/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday-the-two-popes-and-the-aeronauts.html', 'snippet': 'A new drama with Anthony Hopkins and Jonathan Pryce is now on Netflix. On Amazon? An adventure movie with Felicity Jones and Eddie Redmayne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE TWO POPES (2019) Stream on Netflix. Holy men bond, quarrel and drink Fanta in this papal dramedy, which casts two seasoned British actors — Anthony Hopkins and Jonathan Pryce — as Catholic leaders with clashing social beliefs. Directed by Fernando Meirelles (“The Constant Gardener”) from a screenplay by Anthony McCarten (“Bohemian Rhapsody”), the movie focuses on the relationship between Pope Benedict XVI (Hopkins) and the future Pope Francis, Jorge Bergoglio (Pryce), during a period when Benedict was nearing retirement and Bergoglio was moving toward becoming his successor. “‘The Two Popes’ is really three movies: a behind-the-scenes tale of Vatican politics, a mini-biopic about the current pontiff, and a two-man study of friendship, rivalry and major British acting,” A.O. Scott wrote in his review for The New York Times. “The first, though intriguing, is more puzzling than illuminating. The second feels a bit like a Wikipedia page, albeit one with first-rate cinematography. The third is absolutely riveting, a subtle and engaging double portrait that touches on complicated matters of faith, ambition and moral responsibility.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/arts/20tvcol-twopopes/merlin_164868852_1bfc68a4-f644-4f19-b724-e8da3af9c0e2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/20/arts/20tvcol-twopopes/merlin_164868852_1bfc68a4-f644-4f19-b724-e8da3af9c0e2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/arts/20tvcol-twopopes/merlin_164868852_1bfc68a4-f644-4f19-b724-e8da3af9c0e2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/arts/20tvcol-twopopes/merlin_164868852_1bfc68a4-f644-4f19-b724-e8da3af9c0e2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/20/arts/20tvcol-twopopes/20tvcol-twopopes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/20/arts/20tvcol-twopopes/20tvcol-twopopes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'