 person. It’s almost like a godlike power.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Outrage Erupts as a Governor Issues Pardons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-21T03:22:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4444d8fe-5761-5955-8b38-64e0520708a9', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4444d8fe-5761-5955-8b38-64e0520708a9'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, Dec. 21, 2019.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/20/pageoneplus/corrections-dec-21-2019.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, Dec. 21, 2019.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Friday about the haggling and eventual agreement between congressional Democrats and the Trump Administration over the new North American trade deal misstated the stance of Representative Terri A. Sewell of Alabama on past trade deals. It is not true that she had never voted on a trade deal. The article also misstated the timing of a conversation Speaker Nancy Pelosi’s office had with Robert Lighthizer, the country’s top trade negotiator, and when Ms. Pelosi told the Democratic caucus “We ate their lunch.” Ms. Pelosi’s office informed Mr. Lighthizer of a news conference late Monday, not Tuesday, and the speaker talked to her caucus on Tuesday, not Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: Dec. 21, 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-21T03:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/656a3e04-e02e-5e52-bc6b-3c0039bc6bac', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/656a3e04-e02e-5e52-bc6b-3c0039bc6bac'}, {'abstract': 'The couple were introduced by a Manhattan family court referee in 2015. The groom was assigned to serve as the bride’s court-appointed lawyer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/21/fashion/weddings/from-all-business-to-romance.html', 'snippet': 'The couple were introduced by a Manhattan family court referee in 2015. The groom was assigned to serve as the bride’s court-appointed lawyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kristin Maria Cahill and James Ernest Iñiguez were married Dec. 21 at the Atelier Ballroom in Jersey City, N.J. Jaimee Lynn Nelson, a Universal Life minister and a friend of the couple, officiated.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/fashion/weddings/22CAHILL-mini/22CAHILL-mini-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/fashion/weddings/22CAHILL-mini/22CAHILL-mini-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/fashion/weddings/22CAHILL-mini/22CAHILL-mini-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/fashion/weddings/22CAHILL-mini/22CAHILL-mini-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1492, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio