raph': 'The Ask Watching column last Sunday misstated the location where the television show “Claws” is set. It is in Manatee County, Fla., not Miami. The error was repeated in a picture caption. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: Dec. 22, 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-22T05:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5670b0bc-4fe2-5839-ac7b-bee28c6c0d39', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5670b0bc-4fe2-5839-ac7b-bee28c6c0d39'}, {'abstract': 'After four seasons, USA Network’s cybersecurity thriller comes to an end. And a Christmas movie from Disney+ is available to stream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/22/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday-mr-robot-and-noelle.html', 'snippet': 'After four seasons, USA Network’s cybersecurity thriller comes to an end. And a Christmas movie from Disney+ is available to stream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MR. ROBOT 9 p.m. on USA Network. This month, Rami Malek earned his third Golden Globe nomination for his lead role as the tortured vigilante hacker in this cyberthriller series. Elliot (Malek) and Mr. Robot (Christian Slater) have come a long way. In last week’s episode (spoiler alert!), Elliot and Whiterose (BD Wong) shared their vision for humanity in a tense philosophical debate before the creation of a seemingly parallel universe. And, if that weren’t enough of a cliffhanger, Elliot came face to face with his hooded doppelgänger and asked the burning question: “Who are you?” Catch the reveal in this two-part series finale.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/arts/22tvcol-mrrobot/22tvcol-mrrobot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/22/arts/22tvcol-mrrobot/22tvcol-mrrobot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/arts/22tvcol-mrrobot/22tvcol-mrrobot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/arts/22tvcol-mrrobot/22tvcol-mrrobot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/arts/22tvcol-mrrobot/22tvcol-mrrobot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/22/arts/22tvcol-mrrobot/22tvcol-mrrobot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/22/arts/22tvcol-mrrobot/22tvcol-mrrobot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Sunday: ‘Mr. Robot’ and ‘Noelle’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-22T06:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection