d0960c-7f52-592f-971d-6c443dc2624a'}, {'abstract': 'A new investment standard would reward efforts to protect tropical forests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/24/opinion/amazon-deforestation.html', 'snippet': 'A new investment standard would reward efforts to protect tropical forests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I moved to the Amazon “Wild West” town of Paragominas in northern Brazil in 1984 as a young scientist studying forest recovery on abandoned pastures, I expected a town filled with bandits and land grabbers. Instead, what I mostly found were courageous, hard-working families from across Brazil who had come to the rugged town of sawmills, cattle ranches and smallholder settlements to improve their lot in life.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/opinion/24nepstad1/merlin_162439044_41608130-a676-4c18-a737-a5cf101fe8e3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/24/opinion/24nepstad1/merlin_162439044_41608130-a676-4c18-a737-a5cf101fe8e3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/opinion/24nepstad1/merlin_162439044_41608130-a676-4c18-a737-a5cf101fe8e3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/opinion/24nepstad1/merlin_162439044_41608130-a676-4c18-a737-a5cf101fe8e3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/opinion/24nepstad1/24n