', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of our goals is to get you up to speed quickly, recapping the biggest headlines and offering a look ahead to the major stories that we’re covering that day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/26/multimedia/26special-px/26special-px-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/26/multimedia/26special-px/26special-px-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/26/multimedia/26special-px/26special-px-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/26/multimedia/26special-px/26special-px-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/26/multimedia/26special-px/26special-px-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/26/multimedia/26special-px/26special-px-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/26/multimedia/26special-px/26special-px-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Morning Briefing: Standouts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-26T04:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Briefings Team', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Briefings Team'}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/196f1f72-b16e-55d0-95ba-85aa911ad813', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/196f1f72-b16e-55d0-95ba-85aa911ad813'}, {'abstract': 'The soapy serial-killer series “You” returns on Netflix. And Céline Sciamma’s “Girlhood” is streaming on Criterion Channel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/26/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday-you-and-girlhood.html', 'snippet': 'The soapy serial-killer series “You” returns on Netflix. And Céline Sciamma’s “Girlhood” is streaming on Criterion Channel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU Stream on Netflix. “Love has taken me to dark places,” the charming serial killer Joe Goldberg (Penn Badgley) says early in the new season of this series. “But Los Angeles has got to be as dark as it gets.” Originally a Lifetime series, “You” picked up steam near the beginning of the year after its first season became available on Netflix. That season played something like “Dexter” crossed with a soap opera: It followed Joe, a killer, as he pursued a romantic obsession in New York City (the relationship didn’t pan out). The new, second season moves the action to the West Coast. It gives Joe a job at a gourmet market and a fresh fixation: a co-worker played by Victoria Pedretti. “The new location allows the showrunner, Sera Gamble, and her staff to add Southern California stereotypes to the generational and class formulas that draw Joe’s scorn,” Mike Hale wrote in his review of the second season for The New York Times, “and to throw the Hollywood melodrama into the genre blender along with the rom-com.” He called the show “one of television’s more addictive treats.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None