name': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/56d8ff87-56b3-590e-b5b0-aec58a36d3cd', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56d8ff87-56b3-590e-b5b0-aec58a36d3cd'}, {'abstract': 'Their breakthroughs were in law, science, music and business, and, like the more famous who died this year, they left indelible legacies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/26/obituaries/in-a-year-of-notable-deaths-a-world-of-women-who-shattered-ceilings.html', 'snippet': 'Their breakthroughs were in law, science, music and business, and, like the more famous who died this year, they left indelible legacies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost all were born between the world wars, one even before women had the right to vote. They came from white-collar homes and blue-, from black households and white. But when they died this year, they had something in common besides the final leveling that death brings. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/27/obituaries/27obityear-abram/merlin_161362020_880fa6dc-7a49-4334-bdad-3505e7ec25a4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/27/obituaries/27obityear-abram/merlin_161362020_880fa6dc-7a49-4334-bdad-3505e7ec25a4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 753}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/27/obituaries/27obityear-abram/merlin_161362020_880fa6dc-7a49-4334-bdad-3505e7ec25a4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 816, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'