odriguez. (Mr. Rodriguez was the photographer for the article.)', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: Dec. 28, 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-28T04:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/6486466d-bf2b-53c6-b91c-3b6a7de38029', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6486466d-bf2b-53c6-b91c-3b6a7de38029'}, {'abstract': 'The live-action Pokémon feature, starring Ryan Reynolds, airs on HBO. And Sam Mendes’s feature directorial debut is available to stream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday-pokemon-detective-pikachu-and-american-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'The live-action Pokémon feature, starring Ryan Reynolds, airs on HBO. And Sam Mendes’s feature directorial debut is available to stream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POKÉMON DETECTIVE PIKACHU (2019) 8 p.m. on HBO; stream on HBO platforms. The first live-action movie based on the Pokemon franchise is sure to please fans of the video game series — less so film buffs. Tim (Justice Smith) arrives in Ryme City, where Pokémon and humans coexist, after his father, who is a detective, seemingly died in a car accident. He meets the fuzzy and adorable title character (voiced by an amusing Ryan Reynolds), who suspects Tim’s father may not be dead. The pair team up with a young journalist (Kathryn Newton) and search the city’s seedy streets for answers. The movie, directed by Rob Letterman, places colorful Pokémon creatures in a neo-noir ascetic, a juxtaposition that recalls “Who Framed Roger Rabbit” (1988). While that adds some visual eye-candy, most critics have said the film could have used a more ambitious plot.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/28/arts/28tvcol-pokemon/merlin_155448636_8f64fae6-50ec-428c-a94a-66f5a9370587-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/28/arts/28tvcol-pokemon/merlin_155448636_8f64fae6-50ec-428c-a94a-66f5a9370587-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/28/arts/28tvcol-pokemon/merlin_155448636_8f64fae6-50ec-428c-a94a-66f5a9370587-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/28/arts/28tvcol-pokemon/merlin_155448636_8f64fae6-50ec-428c-a94a-66f5a9370587-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/28/arts/28tvcol-pokemon/merlin_155448636_8f64fae6-50ec-428c-a94a-66f5a9370587-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/28/arts/28tvcol-pokemon/merlin_155448636_8f64fae6-50ec-428c-a94a-66f5a9370587-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/28/arts/28tvcol-pokemon/merlin_155448636_8f64fae6-50ec-428c-a94a-66f5a9370587-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday: ‘Pokémon Detective Pikachu’