ole': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03b51a60-d125-5fca-a60a-91374073cc22', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03b51a60-d125-5fca-a60a-91374073cc22'}, {'abstract': 'A truck filled with explosives blew up at a busy intersection in the capital. It was the latest, and the worst, in a series of recent attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/28/world/africa/somalia-explosion-mogadishu.html', 'snippet': 'A truck filled with explosives blew up at a busy intersection in the capital. It was the latest, and the worst, in a series of recent attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia — An explosives-laden truck blew up at a busy intersection in the Somali capital on Saturday and killed at least 79 people, the latest sign of resurgent militant activity in a country plagued by an enduring strain of violent extremism.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somalia Bombing Kills Nearly 80, Raising Fears of Resurgent Militancy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nearly 80 Die As Blast Strikes Somali Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mogadishu (Somalia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-28T09:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hussein Mohamed, Abdi Latif Dahir and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hussein', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohamed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abdi', 'middlename': 'Latif', 'lastname': 'Dahir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/351b0ed2-5d28-538c-aa98-8125c5dbe2a7', 'word_count': 1427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/351b0ed2-5d28-538c-aa98-8125c5dbe2a7'}, {'abstract': 'Your lease probably includes a clause prohibiting alterations. But do not despair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/28/realestate/can-i-renovate-my-rental-apartment.html', 'snippet': 'Your lease probably includes a clause prohibiting alterations. But do not despair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q: For more than a decade, we’ve lived in a rent-stabilized apartment in Forest Hills, Queens. In all this time, the landlord has never made any improvements to the apartment. As tenants, we’ve made minor improvements — painted the apartment twice, painted the trim, and replaced light fixtures and bathroom fixtures. When we moved in, the kitchen cabinets were brand-new. Although they’re in good condition, they look dated and we’d like to paint them white to improve the look and make a dark kitchen appear lighter. Can we do this, or would we get in trouble with the landlord?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/29/realestate/29ASK/merlin_166356243_6c577006-5302-48c6-ab44-393be0ee98a5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/29/realestate/29ASK/merlin_166356243_6c577006-5302-48c6-ab44-393be0ee98a5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 118}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumb