constructors toss one out every once in a while (Alex Eaton-Salners, David Steinberg and Sam Ezersky, recently). I thought that Peter Gordon (a prolific contributor to the regular puzzle) was following suit, but it turns out that he had a bunch of these in the early ’00s, when you could solve a diagramless puzzle every six weeks or so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Diagramless', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Peter (Crossword Constructor)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-28T16:40:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46041ec9-dfac-56d9-a788-fdc3434f5a6e', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46041ec9-dfac-56d9-a788-fdc3434f5a6e'}, {'abstract': 'Harvey Fierstein, Betty Buckley and more on the sunny songwriter behind “Hello, Dolly!” and “Mame,” who hoped that even a flop would find a second life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/28/theater/remembering-jerry-herman-harvey-fierstein-chita-rivera.html', 'snippet': 'Harvey Fierstein, Betty Buckley and more on the sunny songwriter behind “Hello, Dolly!” and “Mame,” who hoped that even a flop would find a second life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everyone described Jerry Herman as an optimist. And certainly the Broadway songwriter, who died Thursday at 88, had reason to look on the bright side: “Hello, Dolly!,” “Mame” and “La Cage aux Folles,” to name his biggest hits, each ran for more than 1,500 performances, the last winning the best musical Tony Award three times (twice for its revivals). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/27/arts/27herman-remember3/merlin_120902699_93f73f4c-c741-4cef-8b5d-8998fc5aaeb4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/27/arts/27herman-remember3/merlin_120902699_93f73f4c-c741-4cef-8b5d-8998fc5aaeb4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/27/arts/27herman-remember3/merlin_120902699_93f73f4c-c741-4cef-8b5d-8998fc5aaeb4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/27/arts/27herman-remember3/merlin_120902699_93f73f4c-c741-4cef-8b5d-8998fc5aaeb4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1408, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/27/arts/27herman-remember3/27herman-remember3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/27/arts/27herman-remember3/27herman-remember3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/27/arts/27herman-remember3/27herman-remember3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Jerry Herman: ‘He Called His Shows His Children’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering a Songwriter and His ‘Children’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herman, Jerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hello, Dolly! (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mack & Mabel (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'La Cage aux Folles (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mame (Play)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-28T16:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af1966f9-151e-5bdb-a9df-ce0d8fe04ed7', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af1966f9-151e-5bdb-a9df-ce0d8fe04ed7'}, {'abstract': 'Readers discuss David Brooks’s rejection of his early socialist ideas, how to get Americans to love capitalism and Finland’s success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/28/opinion/letters/socialism-capitalism.html', 'snippet': 'Readers discuss David Brooks’s rejection of his early socialist ideas, how to get Americans to love capitalism and Finland’s success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/opinion/05brooks1/merlin_137656854_99cf7736-a13a-43db-bfc1-e7432bf058ab-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop