ections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-12-29T05:52:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/b82586e1-603d-5eb5-bc47-4aa01f9f98f7', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b82586e1-603d-5eb5-bc47-4aa01f9f98f7'}, {'abstract': 'A new mystery series about a high school cheerleading squad arrives on USA Network. And a dance-themed dating show debuts on Fox.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/29/arts/television/dare-me-flirty-dancing.html', 'snippet': 'A new mystery series about a high school cheerleading squad arrives on USA Network. And a dance-themed dating show debuts on Fox.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DARE ME 10 p.m. on USA Network. This new mystery series is based on the 2013 novel of the same name, which The New York Times Book Review described as a cross between “Heathers” and “Fight Club.” High school cheerleaders Beth (Marlo Kelly) and Addy (Herizen F. Guardiola) have been inseparable for years. When the team’s new, young coach, Colette (Willa Fitzgerald), settles into the school and clicks with Addy, Beth (the bossy one) feels threatened. She tries to keep a tight grip on the team and her friendship, but things only go downhill. Then, the drama reaches a fever pitch after a suspicious death leads to an investigation into Colette and the cheerleading team. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/29/arts/29tvcol-dare/29tvcol-dare-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/29/arts/29tvcol-dare/29tvcol-dare-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jum