pub_date': '2019-12-30T22:18:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nita Lowey and David Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f662347-079d-5f33-be8d-af177726c47a', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f662347-079d-5f33-be8d-af177726c47a'}, {'abstract': 'At Silver Moon Bakery on the Upper West Side, the French-style Epiphany cake gets an upgrade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/30/dining/king-cake-silver-moon-bakery.html', 'snippet': 'At Silver Moon Bakery on the Upper West Side, the French-style Epiphany cake gets an upgrade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year Judith Norell, an owner of Silver Moon Bakery on the Upper West Side, has added a new twist, raspberry preserves, to her galette des rois, or king cake, the confection served for Epiphany on Jan. 6. It’s usually fashioned from puff pastry and filled with marzipan, with a good luck token hidden inside. Her slightly nubbly homemade marzipan interior now has the added richness of raspberry and includes a tiny ceramic figurine embedded in it. She noted that some people serve the cake for New Year’s Eve.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner3/30burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner3/30burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner3/30burner3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner3/30burner3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1224, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner3/30burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner3/30burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner3/30burner3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A King Cake With a Raspberry Twist', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Celebrate: A King Cake With a Raspberry Twist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Moon Bakery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-30T22:23:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e951a1-c9d1-583d-ae9d-34d5e8236073', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e951a1-c9d1-583d-ae9d-34d5e8236073'}, {'abstract': 'Paski Sir, made from sheep’s milk from the Croatian island of Pag, has a nutty aroma and a honeyed aftertaste.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/30/dining/croatian-cheese-paski-sir.html', 'snippet': 'Paski Sir, made from sheep’s milk from the Croatian island of Pag, has a nutty aroma and a honeyed aftertaste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many more sheep than humans live on the windswept Croatian island of Pag in the Adriatic Sea. The sheep, a breed called paska ovka, graze on the landscape, and their milk takes on the briny tang of the environment in a local cheese called Paski Sir. This fairly firm-textured cheese, with a nutty aroma and a sharpness mellowed by a honeyed aftertaste, has now been given protected geographic status by the European Union. It’s made in wheels of about 5 pounds, and usually sold in smaller wedges. In Croatia, it’s often served cut in chunks and drizzled with olive oil.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner1/30burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner1/30burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner1/30burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner1/30burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner1/30burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner1/30burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner1/30burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Add This Cheese to Your Party Board', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Slice: Add This Cheese To Your Party Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sheep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-30T22:25:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3648ca30-60c3-562c-ae93-9b0331925477', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3648ca30-60c3-562c-ae93-9b0331925477'}, {'abstract': 'Blue Moon Acres is growing five styles of rice in accordance with Korean farming practices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/30/dining/new-jersey-rice-blue-moon-acres.html', 'snippet': 'Blue Moon Acres is growing five styles of rice in accordance with Korean farming practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'California and South Carolina are the usual sources for American-grown rice, but you can add New Jersey to the list. In Pennington, southwest of New Brunswick, Blue Moon Acres is cultivating assorted rices. There are medium- and long-grain brown rice; white sushi rice; a mix of short-grain brown and black rice, called black and tan, that turns purplish when cooked; and an Italian rice, short-grain Maratelli, for risotto and paella. The rices are husked to order and delivered very fresh, so they often need slightly shorter cooking times than recommended. They are grown according to Korean natural farming techniques that encourage the growth of healthy microorganisms in the soil to eliminate the need for chemical applications. They are also said to be uncontaminated by heavy metals like arsenic, which have been found in some rice crops.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner7/30burner7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner7/30burner7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner7/30burner7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner7/30burner7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1289, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner7/30burner7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner7/30burner7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner7/30burner7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey, Now Known for Rice', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Simmer: The Garden State Is Now Known for Rice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Moon Acres', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-30T22:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7609214-191d-50ce-8789-ada1ec32962e', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7609214-191d-50ce-8789-ada1ec32962e'}, {'abstract': 'The Chicago restaurant teamed up with the distiller Rhine Hall for this sippable tipple.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/30/dining/rhine-hall-coffee-liqueur.html', 'snippet': 'The Chicago restaurant teamed up with the distiller Rhine Hall for this sippable tipple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rhine Hall is a fruit brandy distiller in the Fulton Market district of Chicago. The company, the outgrowth of a backyard hobby, now makes more than a dozen brandies and similar products. About a year ago, it teamed up with Alinea, the three Michelin-star restaurant in Chicago, to create a coffee liqueur. Made from handpicked beans infused in pineapple brandy, with vanilla beans added, the coffee liqueur delivers bright, lightly acidic coffee flavor and some sweetness without being syrupy. Sip it on the rocks after dinner, use it in cocktails or to drench gingerbread. Until a couple of months ago, it was available only at Alinea and its sibling bar, the Aviary, but now wine and liquor stores have it. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner2/merlin_166054575_fab96874-595e-4438-a8cc-1b4f06ba64ca-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner2/merlin_166054575_fab96874-595e-4438-a8cc-1b4f06ba64ca-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 791}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner2/merlin_166054575_fab96874-595e-4438-a8cc-1b4f06ba64ca-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner2/merlin_166054575_fab96874-595e-4438-a8cc-1b4f06ba64ca-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1555, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner2/30burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner2/30burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner2/30burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alinea Had a Hand in This Coffee Liqueur', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: Acclaimed Restaurant Helped Create a Liqueur', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alinea (Chicago, Ill, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rhine Hall Distillery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-30T22:38:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcf4e942-ac6a-5f48-89e7-d0638ec25330', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcf4e942-ac6a-5f48-89e7-d0638ec25330'}, {'abstract': '“The Corn Exchange Cookbook” may look homey, but there are many lessons here.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/30/dining/corn-exchange-cookbook.html', 'snippet': '“The Corn Exchange Cookbook” may look homey, but there are many lessons here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its homespun snapshots, “The Corn Exchange Cookbook” is not exactly a lavish gift book, but its pages promise to become stained and dog-eared from frequent use. MJ Adams — a New York chef who worked with Tom Valenti, David Page and Edna Lewis — moved to Rapid City, S.D., in 1996 after a family tragedy and opened a shop, then a bistro, the Corn Exchange, which received some national notice and closed after 15 years. Her dishes are those you’d be likely to prepare daily, for family and guests. Along the way she subtly instructs. Pay attention, and you’ll learn basic soupmaking. Her soups follow a similar method, starting with diced pot vegetables, then the key ingredients and the liquid. Blue cheese and potato tarts, Moroccan lamb shanks with couscous and feta, buffalo short ribs and a fragrant nutmeg cake are some other fine recipes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner6/30burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner6/30burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 691}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner6/30burner6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 890, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner6/30burner6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1780, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner6/30burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner6/30burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/01/dining/30burner6/30burner6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cookbook You’ll Turn to Again and Again', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Prepare: Cookbook Contains Valuable Lessons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rapid City (SD)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, MJ (Chef)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Corn Exchange Cookbook (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-30T22:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d291edf1-aff7-5a71-a440-0f7c52617e4a', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d291edf1-aff7-5a71-a440-0f7c52617e4a'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know at the end of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/30/briefing/texas-nfl-carlos-ghosn.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know at the end of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': '(Want to get this briefing by email? Here’s the sign-up.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/30/briefing/123019evening-briefing-promo/30evening-briefing-slide-7CYI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/30/briefing/123019evening-briefing-promo/30evening-briefing-slide-7CYI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/30/briefing/123019evening-briefing-promo