rta in the dead of winter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The divemaster rattled a shaker to get my attention and I spun around, wondering if something was wrong. Out of the deep blue a set of shadows quickly became a pod of bottlenose dolphins performing corkscrews and back flips as they approached, emphasizing how at ease they were compared to us, with our air tanks, weight belts and fins. And then, when they were within an arm’s reach, they took turns rolling over for belly rubs.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Year of Abrupt Transitions, a Trip to Tahiti. And Calgary.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Ocean Breezes to the Chinook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diving and Divers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snohetta', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Calgary (Alberta)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahiti', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-31T10:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebastian Modak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebastian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Modak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82b353ae-f53d-5ec2-8c39-4aa673318c00', 'word_count': 2146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82b353ae-f53d-5ec2-8c39-4aa673318c00'}, {'abstract': 'In one Los Angeles home, it’s difficult to tell. And that’s th