y than any movie has in years. The actor plays Frank Sheeran, an elderly hit man looking back on his life. It has been a long one — the film runs some 209 minutes. After 28 of them, we’ve reached the 1950s, and a 30-something Sheeran has just learned that a neighborhood grocer shoved his daughter. This younger Sheeran is still played by the 76-year-old De Niro; digital effects have been used to take years off his face, a technique that’s applied to a few actors as the film moves through time. And it’s this curiously smooth De Niro who marches the daughter back to the store, throws the grocer to the curb and stomps repeatedly on his hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/magazine/05mag-screenland-1/05mag-screenland-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/01/05/magazine/05mag-screenland-1/05mag-screenland-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/magazine/05mag-screenland-1/05mag-screenland-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/magazine/05mag-screenland-1/05mag-screenland-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/magazine/05mag-screenland-1/05mag-screenland-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/01/05/magazine/05mag-screenland-1/05mag-screenland-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/01/05/magazine/05mag-screenland-1/05mag-screenland-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Most Ridiculous Part of ‘The Irishman’ Actually Works', 'kicker': 'Screenland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Niro, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Irishman (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-12-31T16:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nitsuh Abebe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nitsuh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abebe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c072243-8779-54d9-b66a-2d5069bd9713', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c072243-8779-54d9-b66a-2d5069bd9713'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Susan Collins of Maine joined Lisa Murkowski in raising concerns over her leaders’ approach, and said she would be “open” to calling witnesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/31/us/politics/susan-collins-impeachment-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Susan Collins of Maine joined Lisa Murkowski in raising concerns over her leaders’ approach, and said she would be “open” to calling witnesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON —\xa0Senator Susan Collins, Republican of Ma